<section id="projects">
  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    A selection of projects I've designed, built, and contributed to.
  </p>

  <div class="projects-grid">
    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>Moody: Colors That Speak</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">AAC · Accessibility</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        An AAC (Augmentative and Alternative Communication) app designed
        to support communication through ARASAAC pictograms, accompanied
        by an ESP32-based wearable prototype for expressing emotional
        states. Selected among the Top 5 nationally at ExpoTécnica 2025
        from 60+ competing projects.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>PJGYS 2026</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">Web · Civic tech</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Web platform developed for Parlamento Joven Guía y Scout Costa
        Rica 2026, used to publish and organize 11 legislative proposals
        with PDF viewing, search, filtering, and progress tracking. I also
        authored Proposal #6 on communicative accessibility in public
        spaces, which was selected by my fraction.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>Sumobot competition</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">Robotics</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Autonomous sumo-fighting robot built on an ESP32-based board with
        CircuitPython. The team competed at Maker Faire San José in two
        consecutive editions, alongside 190+ participating teams each
        year. I maintain the embedded codebase and help mentor incoming
        teammates.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>Aion: Academic Information &amp; Opportunity Network</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">Web · Community</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        A student-led web platform I helped build to connect a school
        community of 1,000+ learners with academic and leadership
        opportunities. More than 50 opportunities have been organized and
        published so far, combining student-submitted listings with
        stories and practical information.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>PytoClicker</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">Python · Desktop</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        A lightweight Python autoclicker built with Tkinter, featuring
        configurable clicking, hotkey controls, and a minimal desktop
        interface. The project was also an exercise in restructuring a
        small application into a cleaner class-based architecture.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-tile">
      <div class="project-tile-head">
        <h3>Lyrics Reader</h3>
        <span class="project-tag">Python · Desktop · API</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        A desktop utility for finding and reading song lyrics one line at
        a time. It checks a local JSON cache before querying LRCLIB,
        supports Unicode lyrics, and includes keyboard controls for moving
        through each verse.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="project-note">
    Links for the ones I've made public are under the sumobot menu in the
    home section — not all of these are open-source yet.
  </p>
</section>
